<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
		The `MINIKeyboard MAS` target. The sandbox and USB devices come from the build settings
		(ENABLE_APP_SANDBOX, ENABLE_RESOURCE_ACCESS_USB in MINIKeyboard-MAS.xcconfig); this file adds
		what they can't.

		The 1189:8890's configuration interface has no HID driver, so the app opens it through
		IOUSBHost — and the sandbox refuses IOUSBHost's user client even with USB devices allowed.
		This exception lets the app open it as the Developer ID build does.

		(Xcode's capability editor rewrites this file and strips comments.)
	-->
	<key>com.apple.security.temporary-exception.iokit-user-client-class</key>
	<array>
		<string>AppleUSBHostFrameworkInterfaceClient</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
